# Commit and push

- After any code change, commit and push in the same turn with `git push origin HEAD:main` (local `master` tracks `origin/main`). Never ask first, never leave unpushed commits, never force-push.
- If the user says "push this" or similar, push immediately — even if you think it was already pushed — and report the result.
- PowerShell: pass the commit message with a here-string, not bash HEREDOC.
- Do not skip hooks. Do not update git config.

# Contact lookup boundaries

- Contact lookup is for reaching the current homeowner of the pinned house (public listing / assessor-style sources). Do not skip-trace personal Google/Facebook accounts, profile photos, or people-search pages of former residents.
